\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Per-pixel signed $\sigma _{\rm  from\,half}$ for the chirality-relevant matched-spiral subsample at NSIDE=32 (Mollweide projection, equatorial coordinates). The observed $|\sigma |^{\rm  obs}_{\max }\!=\!4.13$ vs the label-shuffle null $|\sigma |^{\rm  null,\,p99}_{\max }\!=\!4.78$ gives a look-elsewhere $p\!=\!0.135$; no NSIDE returns $p\!<\!0.05$. The map shows no coherent large-scale structure beyond random pixel-level scatter; the high-$|\sigma |$ pixels are isolated rather than clustered, consistent with the counting-statistics distribution expected from label-shuffle.}}{8}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:healpix_skymap}{{4}{8}{Per-pixel signed $\sigma _{\rm from\,half}$ for the chirality-relevant matched-spiral subsample at NSIDE=32 (Mollweide projection, equatorial coordinates). The observed $|\sigma |^{\rm obs}_{\max }\!=\!4.13$ vs the label-shuffle null $|\sigma |^{\rm null,\,p99}_{\max }\!=\!4.78$ gives a look-elsewhere $p\!=\!0.135$; no NSIDE returns $p\!<\!0.05$. The map shows no coherent large-scale structure beyond random pixel-level scatter; the high-$|\sigma |$ pixels are isolated rather than clustered, consistent with the counting-statistics distribution expected from label-shuffle}{figure.4}{}}
