\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces V-Web (left) vs Tempel+2014 FoF (right) cross-validation: per-class CW fraction with $95\%$ Jeffreys binomial credible intervals, shared y-axis [0.43, 0.53]. Dashed reference is parity $f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.5$; dotted-red reference is the Paper~IV global $\bar  f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.4974$ classifier-monopole offset. The highest-$n$ concordance is the filament class pair: V-Web filament $f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.4980$ ($n\!=\!408{,}187$) vs Tempel filament\_like $f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.4982$ ($n\!=\!14{,}317$) differ by $0.026$\,percentage points, well below the $0.2$\,pp concordance spec (supporting, not load-bearing; the primary cross-classifier validation is the on-DESI DESIVAST re-projection in \S  \ref {sec:tweb_compare}). Lower-$n$ classes scatter by counting statistics and classifier-definition mismatch (V-Web $\lambda _{\rm  th}\!=\!0$ vs Tempel discrete richness thresholds) but do not contradict the environmental-independence headline.}}{10}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tempel_overlay}{{6}{10}{V-Web (left) vs Tempel+2014 FoF (right) cross-validation: per-class CW fraction with $95\%$ Jeffreys binomial credible intervals, shared y-axis [0.43, 0.53]. Dashed reference is parity $f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.5$; dotted-red reference is the Paper~IV global $\bar f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.4974$ classifier-monopole offset. The highest-$n$ concordance is the filament class pair: V-Web filament $f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.4980$ ($n\!=\!408{,}187$) vs Tempel filament\_like $f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.4982$ ($n\!=\!14{,}317$) differ by $0.026$\,percentage points, well below the $0.2$\,pp concordance spec (supporting, not load-bearing; the primary cross-classifier validation is the on-DESI DESIVAST re-projection in \S \ref {sec:tweb_compare}). Lower-$n$ classes scatter by counting statistics and classifier-definition mismatch (V-Web $\lambda _{\rm th}\!=\!0$ vs Tempel discrete richness thresholds) but do not contradict the environmental-independence headline}{figure.6}{}}
